// SWARM RABBIT HOLE — Wave 9 (Impl-N): divergence class 2 made
// executable — negation-through-recursion, the E-ZADM rejection.
//
// The body μy. 1⊖y oscillates: applying ⊖ (negation) through the
// recursive variable makes the body NON-MONOTONE in the recursive
// variable, so Knaster–Tarski does not apply and there is no least
// fixpoint to converge to (W2C §3.3's second named divergence class).
// The failure is the non-monotone BODY, tier-orthogonal — 1⊖y is
// group arithmetic, so this is not a Tier-L vs Tier-G question; no
// carrier choice repairs a body that flips its input.
//
// `zfix_negate` is the surface's negation-through-recursion mode: a
// RECOGNIZED intrinsic that the checker ALWAYS rejects with E-ZADM
// (the same checked-refusal discipline as zfix_count — refusals are
// compile-time errors, never silent divergence, W2C §3.5). This file
// is a compile-FAIL golden case (tests/golden.rs).

fn main() {
    ptr seed = zset_new(0)
    zset_add(seed, 1, 1)
    zfix_negate(seed) // must be rejected: E-ZADM
}
